From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:36:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vieww-text: an example that times the system font scan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The step-by-step startup trace (8f8997f) caught the wait_loop hang on the
affected laptop: the last line before 20 s of silence was `window made
visible`, and `system fonts loaded` never came. Between them are only the
frame log, the frame driver and `driver.use_system_fonts()` — the full
fontdb scan of every font fontconfig lists, run on the main thread before
a window's first frame, in every process.

That fits every observation: it fails on the first scenario after an
11-12 minute build (the build evicts the font files from the page cache;
the same run's window creation took 1.2 s instead of 30 ms), and later
scenarios — and every warm manual run — pass, because the fonts are
cached by then.

examples/font_scan.rs times exactly that scan (fontdb's, and the
FontStore vieww builds), so it can be measured cold and warm on the
machine where it hangs. Here: 130 ms for 238 files on first run, 8 ms
warm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
---
 .../crates/vieww-text/examples/font_scan.rs   | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 vieww_base/crates/vieww-text/examples/font_scan.rs

diff --git a/vieww_base/crates/vieww-text/examples/font_scan.rs b/vieww_base/crates/vieww-text/examples/font_scan.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6569ee5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vieww_base/crates/vieww-text/examples/font_scan.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+//! Time the system font scan `FrameDriver::use_system_fonts` runs before a
+//! window's first frame.
+//!
+//! ```console
+//! cargo run --release -p vieww-text --example font_scan
+//! ```
+//!
+//! Run it twice: the first run after the disk cache was emptied (a reboot, a
+//! long build, or `sync; echo 3 | sudo tee /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches`) is the
+//! cold-start cost a freshly launched application pays; the second is the warm
+//! one. `tests/wait_loop.rs`' idle scenario in `vieww-platform-winit` timed out
+//! inside this scan on a laptop right after an 11-minute build.
+
+use std::time::Instant;
+
+use cosmic_text::fontdb;
+
+fn main() {
+    let start = Instant::now();
+    let mut db = fontdb::Database::new();
+    db.load_system_fonts();
+    let scan = start.elapsed();
+    let faces = db.len();
+    let files: std::collections::HashSet<_> = db
+        .faces()
+        .filter_map(|f| match &f.source {
+            fontdb::Source::File(p) | fontdb::Source::SharedFile(p, _) => Some(p.clone()),
+            fontdb::Source::Binary(_) => None,
+        })
+        .collect();
+    println!(
+        "fontdb scan:            {scan:>10.2?}  ({faces} faces in {} files)",
+        files.len()
+    );
+
+    let start = Instant::now();
+    let _store = vieww_text::FontStore::with_system_fallback();
+    println!(
+        "FontStore (what vieww does before the first frame): {:.2?}",
+        start.elapsed()
+    );
+}
